{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 54, :comments ["<b>This is the Torah for every plague of tzara'at — for the scall, and for the tzara'at of garments and of houses, and for a swelling, and for a scab, and for a bright spot.</b> Even though the tradition received from our Rabbis, of blessed memory, is the truth, and it is what attests to the matters of tzara'at — that first He smites him in his house, so that he may humble his heart and search his deeds and return in repentance; if he repents, well and good, and if not, He smites him in his garment; if he repents, well and good, and if not, He smites him in his very body — the arrangement of the matter is not so in the parashiot. For the parashah of נגע צרעת כי תהיה באדם — 'the plague of tzara'at when it is in a person' — comes first, and after it the parashah of והבגד כי יהיה בו נגע צרעת — 'and the garment when it has a plague of tzara'at' — and after it the parashah of ונתתי נגע צרעת בבית ארץ אחזתכם — 'and I will place a plague of tzara'at in a house of the land of your possession.' And the Torah took this course, for it mentioned first the tzara'at of bodies, and afterward the tzara'at of garments, and after that the tzara'at of houses, because all the ways of the Torah are דרכי נועם — ways of pleasantness — and all her paths are שלום — peace; and so that the arrangement not be ordered as a punishment that goes and intensifies, as the matter actually was, but rather goes and diminishes, as is explained to us in the order of the parashiot."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:28.263885655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}